.TH PISU 1 "2026-09-23" "learning-pi" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pisu \- safely update pi and the learning-system extension packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pisu
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B pi-safe-update
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pisu
is the update gate for the pi learning system. pi and its extension packages
are hard-pinned in
.IR ~/learning-pi/versions.lock.json ;
nothing updates itself.
.B pisu
stages any newer pi and extension-package versions in an isolated sandbox, runs
.BR lpcheck (1)
against that candidate set, and promotes everything only if every learning
behavior invariant still passes. On failure it stays pinned and writes a
diagnosis report. It never patches code.
.PP
.B pi-safe-update
is the full command;
.B pisu
is the short alias installed on
.IR PATH .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR check ", " c " (default)"
Read-only. Reports the pinned and newest pi version and extension-package
versions, and scans the candidate pi changelog for changes to surfaces the
learning layer depends on.
.TP
.BR update ", " up " [\-\-to VER] [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-pi-only]"
Resolve newer pi and package versions, stage them side-by-side, run
.BR lpcheck ,
and promote only on success. Options:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-to VER
Use a specific pi version instead of the newest.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Stage and test, but change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-pi-only
Ignore extension-package updates and consider pi only.
.RE
.TP
.BR doctor ", " dr
Re-run
.B lpcheck
against the currently pinned versions. Use after a hand-run
.B pi update
to detect drift.
.TP
.BR rollback ", " rb
Restore the pi and package versions from the previous promotion recorded in the
journal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B pisu
Show what, if anything, can be updated.
.TP
.B pisu up
Apply all available pi and extension-package updates through the gate.
.TP
.B pisu up \-\-dry-run
See whether the candidate set passes without changing anything.
.TP
.B pisu rollback
Undo the last promotion.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or no update was available.
.TP
.B 1
The candidate failed
.BR lpcheck .
The current pins were kept and a diagnosis was written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Staging error (could not install or build the sandbox).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/learning-pi/versions.lock.json
The pinned pi version, package versions, and the promotion journal.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/learning-pi/diagnosis-*.md
Failure diagnosis reports. Fix them with the
.B pi-diagnosis-fix
opencode skill.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/learning-pi/audit-recent.log
Weekly read-only gate-provenance audit output.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LEARNING_PI_ROOT
Override the learning-pi checkout root.
.TP
.B PI_OFFLINE
When set, the launcher's background availability check is skipped.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lpcheck (1),
.BR pi (1)
.PP
.I ~/learning-pi/CONTRACT.md
and
.I ~/learning-pi/README.md
document the behavior the gate protects and the revise door for intentional
behavior changes.
